quote.p:
1. The presence of very large numbers of foreign students in Western
                        Europe, many of them from key African and other underdeveloped
                        countries;

2. The fact that we have a foreign currency requirement to meet in the
                        program and these currencies are largely available in Europe—practically
                        none are available in Africa and few in Latin America;

4. The existence of Fulbright
                        agreements with most Western European countries which embody commitments to
                        certain levels of programs;
